      "description": "Utah HB 452 — Artificial Intelligence Amendments (Mental Health Chatbots)",
      "weight": 100,
      "data": {
        "official_name": "Utah House Bill 452 — Artificial Intelligence Amendments (Mental Health Chatbots, Utah Code Title 13, Chapter 72a)",
        "common_name": "Utah HB 452 (Mental Health Chatbots)",
        "alternate_names": [
          "Utah Code § 13-72a-101 et seq.",
          "H.B. 452 (2025 General Session)"
        ],
        "description": "Utah statute regulating mental health chatbots that use AI to provide therapeutic or mental health communications: requires clear pre-interaction and recurring disclosure that the chatbot is an AI and not a human therapist, restricts the sale or sharing of individually identifiable health inputs and targeted advertising inside chatbot conversations, and requires documentation of foundation models and crisis guardrails.",
        "notes": "Status: In force May 7, 2025 (signed by Governor Cox March 25, 2025; verified as of 2026-11-03). Enforced by the Utah Division of Consumer Protection and Attorney General.",
        "urls": [
